    "result_text": "Each person's row now has a Statement button, and all 4 Playwright tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**What a statement does**\n- It records the person's due-total, how many of their claims count, and the sheet's today. It writes `STATEMENT sheet=\u2026 by=\u2026 name=\u2026 due-total=\u2026 claims=\u2026` to the audit file.\n- Every claim of theirs that counts is bound to the figure it shows at that moment. A claim that is already bound keeps its bound figure when the next statement rebinds it, not a fresh rate. The spec depends on this: Ada's second statement comes to 9.02 rather than being recalculated at the new rate.\n- A claim that doesn't count when a statement is taken goes back to live. Between statements, a bound claim that gets voided still shows its bound figure and \"yes\".\n- A settled claim keeps its settled figure.\n\n**On screen**\n- Each claim shows stated yes/no (`claim-stated`).\n- Each person shows their statement count, the last statement's due-total and its date (`person-statement-count`, `person-stated-total`, `person-statement-date`). The last two are blank before the first statement.\n- A refused statement shows `person-error` on that row. The error clears on the next action on that row.\n\n**Stored data**\n- A new migration, `V13__statement.sql`, adds a `statement` table and two new claim columns: `stated` and `stated_due`.\n- Statements go in their own table rather than on the person. That way, taking a statement doesn't change the person's version, so it won't make someone's open edit of that person fail as \"changed meanwhile\".\n- The server code is in a new `statement` package. `ClaimService.figureOf` works out the figure a claim currently has.\n\n**Choices the request left open \u2014 worth checking**\n- **Settling a bound claim** fixes it at its bound figure, not the live rate, so its due doesn't jump when it's settled. The spec never settles a bound claim, so this isn't tested.\n- **No rate:** if a claim's figure is n/a when it's bound, it stays bound as n/a. A statement's due-total is recorded as `n/a` under the same rule the screen already uses: the grade has no rate today and no claim keeps a fixed figure. Bound claims now count as keeping a figure in that rule.\n- **Editing a bound claim's amount** leaves its bound figure unchanged until the next statement. The request only mentions rates and grades, so I left it that way.",
